  "description": "KIZCOM crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C50 H104 Mn5 N8 O40 Tb4,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Tb1A (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Mn2A (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn3A (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.825-3.896 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 82.52-132.50°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C54H110Mn5Tb4N10O40. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 Piv (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
